+# GDS1 equal-semantic-work fast-write sham
+
+Source-only successor branch to qualified FULL GDE1 commit
+`2f2cd592ef7a05d199dd1bc3353afdd7f49bcee7`. The qualified branch and tested
+`ed5f2f5a13e9d7b3851272adeeec7c73b605f7aa` remain recoverable. No native
+compilation, test, world interval or scientific seed run has been authorized for
+this extension. Test names below describe desired assertions, not results.
+
+## Meaning of the sham
+
+GDS1 uses the exact GDE1 raw grouped derivative, bounded staged trace, inherited
+receptor projection, delayed trace and candidate fast arithmetic. One shared
+credit core executes them once. The mode is bound in pending state at the actual
+source forward and checked again at staging and sealed credit. FULL calls the
+ApplyFast mode; sham calls SuppressFast. Both consume one pending boundary.
+
+For each declared ActionCandidate/MemoryContext coordinate, both modes compute
+`candidate = bounded_fast_update(F, eta, alpha, receptor_projection, delayed_E)`.
+Both count candidate-versus-current bit changes and commit staged eligibility.
+Only FULL assigns the candidate fast value. Sham neither assigns it nor advances
+weight generation. Decision/outcome timestamps and normal source dispatch still
+advance. This is suppression before assignment, not a write followed by undo,
+a second biological transaction, or an optimizer running in secret.
+
+Typed counts distinguish hypothetical bit changes from applied bit changes.
+FULL's existing receipt fields and serialization remain unchanged; a checked,
+nonpersisted accessor derives its equal hypothetical/applied counts. GDS1 has a
+new receipt carrying both counts, the existing causal receipt fields, and its
+own work-policy identity. New persisted fields are strings/integers, not f64.
+
+The same semantic pullback, trace and candidate-update units are reserved and
+charged in both modes. Those prices do not measure wall time, allocations or
+administrative assignments. The sham has a distinct work identity, not a claim
+that it is the older lower-cost closed policy. Actual arithmetic and charges
+remain once per lived decision, including candidate updates that produce no bit
+change. No rate, source/genes, sampler, controller row or normalization changes.
+
+Only declared eligibility can evolve in the sham. All fast values, lifetime,
+other eligibility, dendritic/structural banks and optimizer moments/ages remain
+closed. Canonical memory/predictor/body behavior is unchanged. The memory-only
+sleep output uses a distinct mode-bound digest domain and the real cycle ID;
+source weight generation stays zero. The existing resident authority hashes the
+entire grouped sidecar, including the sham policy, work identity and controller.
+
+## Admission and preservation
+
+A fresh GDS1 wrapper has a distinct outer byte prefix, lineage, policy,
+controller schema and work identity. Full, closed and sham decoders reject one
+another's prefixes before any JSON/source decoding. The constructor is a fresh
+admission through the same canonical preparation; there is no checkpoint or
+acquired-life conversion API. Enabling either mode on an already mode-tagged or
+executed controller is rejected. Restore checks mode, receipts, generation,
+exact sampler mirrors, sleep output and resident authority.
+
+The optional sham sidecar is omitted when absent. The entire qualified FULL
+wrapper source is unchanged, as are selected legacy/direct bodies and the
+closed literal witness. Shared envelope dispatch and credit code intentionally
+change to admit the new mode, so source identity alone cannot prove FULL byte
+preservation. `scripts/check_grouped_decoder_sham_legacy.py` records narrowly
+scoped exact source witnesses in `LEGACY-SOURCE-WITNESS.json`; it makes no runtime
+claim.
+
+## Authored native gates, all pending
+
+1. Same fresh 240-tick fixture, first actual FULL/sham step: exact source context,
+   receptors, sample, work counters, reservation, body debit, sealed patch and
+   physical receipt. FULL applied changes equal sham hypothetical changes;
+   sham applied changes/generation are zero, with nonzero eligibility. Apart
+   from FULL's allowed fast values/generation, source state must agree. Sampled
+   scores remain pre-update. No equality is required on later divergent lives.
+2. Exact warm/cold sham continuation after acquired traces plus clearly labeled
+   synthetic nonzero recurrent, dendritic/structural and optimizer sentinels.
+   Every fast/lifetime/other-trace sentinel must stay unchanged. A failed late
+   NaN-temperature step must roll back atomically.
+3. Wrong owner/frame/action/sequence/source/dispatch/side/feature/phenotype and
+   receptor-frame checks, wrong FULL-versus-sham credit entry point, duplicate
+   credit, controller conversion, mode-sidecar tampering and cross-mode restore.
+4. Ordinary 1,200-tick preparation and at most 24 native intervals: observe actual
+   BodySleep, nonzero traces, exactly one memory-only consolidation, exact cold
+   continuation, Waking and resumed decisions. Check mode-specific sleep digest
+   and cycle identity. If the event is absent, record the failed bound; do not
+   force actions, retune coefficients or search seeds.
+5. Run affected existing GDE1 and closed compatibility checks, strict lint, and
+   both literal wire witnesses. No broader experiment/cohort is authorized.
+
+## Exact old FULL witness plan
+
+`grouped_full_literal_witness.rs` is a small ignored helper requiring
+`ALIFE_GROUPED_FULL_WITNESS_DIR`. It uses only qualified GDE1 APIs and the existing
+`learning_fixture()` from the old source, temperatures 0.73 and 1.17, and exact
+cold restore after both steps. It exports the full initial envelope, both full
+acquired envelopes and both decision tuples. It also requires actual fast
+changes in the ordinary fixture. None of those state exports belong in the
+source patch or a public artifact.
+
+After a resource/lane grant, compile and run this identical helper on the
+qualified FULL source and on this branch, serially. No additional checkout is
+needed: preserve clean commits, temporarily use a new test-only branch at
+`2f2cd592` in the same worktree, add only the identical helper and its test-module
+line, retain its binary/hashes/output, then return to the new source. Never
+move or alter the qualified branch. Compare all five complete outputs byte for
+byte, not only source activations. The original closed witness remains
+source-identical and can separately compare against its retained exact outputs.
+No old FULL preservation claim is made before that comparison runs.
+
+## Source-review corrections and limits
+
+The first source pass caught the raw-gradient receipt guard still admitting only
+the old FULL controller schema; the guard now admits either explicit learning
+schema while requiring matching native/core identities. The numeric derivative
+is unchanged. This was caught before compilation or execution.
+
+This sham isolates fast-write permission under equal declared semantic learning
+work. It does not isolate per-channel causal reward, remove physiological
+computation costs, demonstrate benefit, make eligibility a full recurrent
+optimizer, or provide GPU/default-game integration. It is not the unrelated
+meal-memory primitive, six-weight taste repair or active recovery study.
+
+Methodological reference: https://rikiyat.github.io/blog/weight-space-programming/
+(targeted repair, whole-controller integration and feedback iteration). Source
+freezing, meaningful failures and eventual validation remain separate milestones.
